WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.568
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:06.405
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:07.507
Welcome.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.708
Well, guys, I have some news

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.376
to make people feel
a little better.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.211
And that is the royal family

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.380
is just as messed up
as everyone else's.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.050
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.353
Yeah, last night,
Oprah sat down with

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.988
Prince Harry and Meghan Markle

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.323
for a two-hour
prime-time special.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.726
I actually thought
it was a great interview.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.295
Obviously, I love Oprah.
She's the best.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:32.531
But good on Meghan Markle for
being brave enough to talk about

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:34.134
her own mental-health struggles

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.435
and all the stuff
she had to deal with.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:39.038
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.274
Yeah, we learned quite a bit

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:44.376
about the rules,
the protocols, the firm.

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:46.679
We even learned that Tyler Perry
took them in

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:50.016
when they came to America
and provided them with security.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.684
Basically, if you missed
the interview,

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.219
the royal family
was like, "Goodbye,"

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.821
and Tyler Perry was like,
"Heller."

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.789
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:00.259
Yeah, last night was an intense
and emotional two hours.

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:02.695
My wife, she walked in
and asked why I was crying.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.598
I was like, "The NBA all-star
game is really good this year."

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.135
"Steph Curry sank
a Mountain Dew ball."

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.471
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.807
Yeah, we learned quite a bit
from the interview,

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.809
like what we've been missing
all year wasn't a normal life.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:17.977
It was Oprah.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.345
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.347
Yeah, it was a big event,
mainly because they revealed

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.215
the baby's gender in California

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:24.983
without burning down
an entire forest.

00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:30.389
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:32.992
Last night, 17 million people
watched the special,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.528
which means the biggest shows
on TV this weekend

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.763
were all about
powerful women and redheads.

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:41.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.536
17 million.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.573
The ratings were so big,
ABC just offered the couple

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.708
their own weekly show
called "Royal-ish."

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:52.145
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.848
Yeah, over 17 million viewers
tuned in.

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:58.184
CBS celebrated until they heard
that more than 600 million

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.253
watched a TikTok about
feta cheese.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:03.089
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.891
If you thought this interview
was big, tune in next Sunday

00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:09.963
when Prince Charles is on "Dr.
Phil" like, "Catch me outside."

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:14.500
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.036
"How about that?

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.338
Catch me outside?"

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.772
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.174
Yeah, Oprah's interview was
such a big ratings success,

00:02:22.174 --> 00:02:24.410
she's already got another
prime-time special in the works.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.312
Check out this promo I saw.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.948
-Oprah is back with
another prime-time interview

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.983
with another powerhouse couple.

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:32.819
-You don't know what
I'm going to ask.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.888
-And it's her most intense...
-What was that conversation?

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.223
-...interview...
-Wait, hold up.

00:02:38.223 --> 00:02:40.727
-...yet.
-So, are you ready?

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:43.028
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.028 --> 00:02:45.631
-Oprah with
Mr. and Mrs. Potato Head.

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:46.932
-Unbelievable.

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:48.834
Mr. and Mrs. Potato Head.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.670
Another big moment during
the interview was when Harry was

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:55.074
asked about his dad,
and he casually mentioned this.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:58.310
-When we were in Canada,
I had three conversations

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.215
with my grandmother and two
conversations with my father

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:05.517
before he stopped
taking my calls.

00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:08.054
-Even worse,
he'd respond to texts with,

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.989
"New mobile, whom is this?"

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:13.392
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:16.395
"New mobile, of whom is this?"

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:18.631
We actually got our hands
on the last phone call

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.333
between Harry
and Prince Charles.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:23.136
It's pretty intense.
Check this out.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.703
-That can't be
a real phone call, right?

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:58.704
Where are we getting that?

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:00.206
That can't be real.
-No way.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:03.609
-Another big revelation was
that Meghan said she and Harry

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:07.646
actually got married three days
before the royal wedding.

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:10.416
Great, now I feel like a fool
for waking up at 5:00 a.m.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.151
to watch two married people
get married.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.919
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:16.589
When she heard about the secret
wedding, the Queen was so upset,

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.357
she asked for
her panini maker back.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:24.029
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.029 --> 00:04:26.131
Yeah, it was
a truly explosive interview

00:04:26.131 --> 00:04:28.801
with shocking revelations that
will stick with us for decades,

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.202
like this one.

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:34.607
-My first job was when I was 13
at a frozen yogurt shop

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.875
called Humphrey Yogart.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.344
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.213
-Even weirder,
Harry worked at a sewing shop

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.848
called Alfred Stitchcock's.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:45.718
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:48.020
Well, guys, let's switch gears
here a little bit.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.757
During a press briefing today,
the director of the CDC

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:53.359
announced new guidelines
for vaccinated Americans.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.627
Watch this.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:57.830
-If you're fully vaccinated
and you're indoors,

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.267
there is no need for masks
or social distancing

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:05.204
if everyone there
is fully vaccinated.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.207
-Oh, man, bingo halls
are about to look like

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.109
a Señor Frog's on spring break.

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.177
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:13.879
Most Americans are like,
"Great news!"

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:16.415
While Texas is like,
"What the hell's a CDC?"

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:22.154
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:25.090
Yeah, you can gather with anyone
who is vaccinated,

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.526
and more importantly,
you can act like a smug A-hole

00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:28.728
around anyone who's not.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:30.163
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:32.398
You can tell things are getting
better because the head of

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.666
the CDC came out and asked

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.600
if anyone wanted the rest
of her breath mint.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.836
Like, "Oh, come on, hey."

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:37.870
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.271
You're taking it too far now.

00:05:39.271 --> 00:05:41.607
"Who wants it? Who wants it?
Huh, huh?"

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:45.912
[ Laughter ]
-Eww!

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:48.247
-That's right.
According to the CDC,

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.448
two weeks
after getting vaccinated --

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:52.217
[ Laughter ]
Did you like that?

00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:53.753
Did you see what I'm saying,
dude?

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:56.022
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.623
That's right.
According to the CDC,

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.057
two weeks
after getting vaccinated,

00:05:59.057 --> 00:06:01.026
grandparents can hug
their grandchildren.

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:02.795
Or as this grandmother put it,

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:05.030
"Yeah, it might be a bit longer
than that."

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:09.602
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.170
Well, guys, everyone is
talking about this.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:14.373
Today, Burger King U.K.
announced a new program

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:18.144
that helps female employees who
are pursuing culinary careers,

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:19.879
but they're getting
a lot of criticism

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:21.114
for how they went about it.

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:23.249
They sent a tweet out that said,

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:25.151
"Women belong in the kitchen."

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.753
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:28.654
-What?

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:31.256
-Anyway, happy International
Women's Day, everyone.

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:34.227
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:37.263
I'm pretty sure one PR person
just flame-broiled their career.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.664
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.966
As soon as it happened, 10,000
people broke their fingers

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:42.334
rushing to be
the first one to tweet,

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:43.903
"What a whopper of a mistake."

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.071
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:48.073
Man, but what a gaffe
for Burger King U.K.

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:50.909
Overall, just a brutal week
for the British royals.

00:06:50.909 --> 00:06:57.115
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:57.115 --> 00:06:59.885
And finally, in Oklahoma,
there's a reward being offered

00:06:59.885 --> 00:07:01.153
for something
pretty interesting.

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:02.321
Listen to this.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:06.058
-A sizable bounty is now
on a legendary figure.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.427
Bigfoot is now
wanted in Oklahoma

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:11.530
for more than $2 million.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.231
-Nice try, Oklahoma.

00:07:13.231 --> 00:07:14.700
You're still not
as crazy as Texas.

